Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::writing_a_block_sends_only_the_block_asked_for`.

The defect: the range check joins its two refusals with `&&`, so a block past the card's end, or
past what the address can name, is sent unless the buffer is also too long for one command.

Expected to fail: the assertion that a write command goes out only when `can_address_blocks`
admits the block.
diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
@@ -572,7 +572,7 @@
     }
     let blocks = (len / BLOCK_BYTES) as u64;
     if blocks > u64::from(u32::MAX) / BLOCK_BYTES as u64
-        || !can_address_blocks(
+        && !can_address_blocks(
             card.blocks,
             card.block_addressed,
             logical_block_address,
